fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-007", author: "user", content: "Implemented as context-aware desugaring (proposal 019 §typing process). Replaced the unconditional 'ListLiteral → cons/nil' rewrite at load.rs:2889-2908 with one keyed on the surrounding entity field type. Touch points: rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/load.rs (convert_term gains a convert_term_with_expected wrapper that propagates Option<TermId> hints; named/positional args now carry the entity field's declared type into the recursive walk via entity_field_types) and rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs (extract_type_param made pub(crate) for reuse). New helper find_list_element_type returns Option<Option<TermId>>: outer Some signals 'desugar here', inner Option carries the element type. Recurses through wrappers (Option[T = List[T = X]]) so the existing implicit-some convention in stage0 facts (e.g. depends_on: Option[T = List[T = String]] written as []) still desugars. Reuses kb::typing::list_to_vec / get_named_arg / extract_type_param rather than re-implementing cons walks. Bare List, parameterized List[T = X], and Option-wrapped List all desugar; Set/Vec/non-list contexts leave ListLiteral as-is for the eval path (eval/eval.rs:629 already builds list values from ListLiteral natively). Tests: 939+ tests in anthill-core all green; github_todo_test (cons/nil patterns over depends_on Option[List]) and eval_m2_test::m2_list_literal_builds_cons_chain still pass; anthill-todo CLI roundtrip verified.", at: "2026-05-04T22:32:59Z")
